{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires","id":1256606,"title":"Why didn't V5 make \"see in the dark\" standard for all vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-22T18:43:11-07:00","id":1256606,"title":"Why didn't V5 make \"see in the dark\" standard for all vampires?","content":"So, I've been informed that V5 didn't take the opportunity to make &quot;see in the dark&quot; a standard ability for all vampires. That's rather surprising to me, as Requiem did it and I've never been able to understand making that exclusive to Protean, especially given how terrified of fire the vampires have been throughout pre-electrical history.<br /> <br /> Is there a good rationale for this? I never got to read Dark Ages, so if there was an explanation there I'm afraid I don't know of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T19:00:05-07:00","id":1256608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires#post1256606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been informed that V5 didn't take the opportunity to make &quot;see in the dark&quot; a standard ability for all vampires. That's rather surprising to me, as Requiem did it and I've never been able to understand making that exclusive to Protean, especially given how terrified of fire the vampires have been throughout pre-electrical history.<br /> <br /> Is there a good rationale for this? I never got to read Dark Ages, so if there was an explanation there I'm afraid I don't know of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is defined anywhere that Vampires have to all see in the dark, and in the modern nights in urban locations it isn't a major issue. It's an easy handwave for your own campaign to just say that the diffuse light emitted by the stars, moon and general ambient lighting in most urban environments (even medieval ones) is enough to allow vampires and humans to get by at nightime without much difficulty, just a bit more inhibited for spotting things out in a distance or heavy shadows. I tend to see the Auspex (Heigtened senses) and Protean (Eyes of the Beast) to be more about seeing in absolute or even supernatural, pitch black darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 09-22-2018, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T22:17:51-07:00","id":1256643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires#post1256606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been informed that V5 didn't take the opportunity to make &amp;quot;see in the dark&amp;quot; a standard ability for all vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the ability to see clearly in the dark (regular dark, not obten) should come stock for every vampire. A successful nocturnal predator, even a supernatural one, should be suited to its environment with all that that entails. I've always thought it really... negligent..that this was not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light inspires illusion and interpretation. Truth can only be found in darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3971-12dollarburrito","name":"12dollarburrito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T23:04:59-07:00","id":1256649,"title":"","content":"It is probably because the writers of the game wanted to try and stick with what the previous editions had established as a definition of a Vampire in their fiction. In the fiction that was established in 1st, 2nd, revised, and v20 vampires could not see in the dark without another power. Even though they could have changed this there seemed to be an effort to keep this definition primarily in tact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T01:18:24-07:00","id":1256657,"title":"","content":"I mean, the ability to see in the &quot;dark&quot; - by starlight and moonlight, not in a sealed space - does come stock for all humans. It's pretty amazing, just go out to the middle of nowhere in the middle of the night and you'll see just fine, clouds or no. So I'd always give vampires the ability to see at least as well as a human when their eyes have adjusted. &quot;Historically&quot; I imagine that's all Kindred needed. It's only after building cities and tombs that they had to start worrying about torches etc. And then the Kindred with protean had an advantage that initially made wild hunting much easier for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T02:54:06-07:00","id":1256672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>12dollarburrito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256643#post1256643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree that the ability to see clearly in the dark (regular dark, not obten) should come stock for every vampire. A successful nocturnal predator, even a supernatural one, should be suited to its environment with all that that entails. I've always thought it really... negligent..that this was not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if not every vampire, at the very least darkness-loving or underground-dwellers like Nosferatu, Setite and Lasombra seem like they should have some means of night vision. Playing a fair amount of Nosferatu, back in the day, I always felt that it was a weird choice for them to be less able to navigate their own underground warrens than a Toreador with Auspex / Heightened Senses. I didn't play a Lasombra, but I would find it similarly dubious that shooting out the light can leave one as lost in the dark as a human, since darkness is kind of their thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T04:06:38-07:00","id":1256682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256657#post1256657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the ability to see in the &quot;dark&quot; - by starlight and moonlight, not in a sealed space - does come stock for all humans. It's pretty amazing, just go out to the middle of nowhere in the middle of the night and you'll see just fine, clouds or no</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit overstated.<br /> <br /> While human night vision is better than most RPG playing people think (because they don't get out in real wild night times a lot), it's pretty different from day vision. There's stuff that works well (and to an extent actually works better), and stuff that works worse, because our senses are complicated like that.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the human eye is fairly well evolved for being prey, not predator, at night. Which means the advantage goes to the mortal, not the vampire. Our motion detection at night is really good, as it's tied to our peripheral vision, which means we lose little in noticing someone trying to sneak up on us to suck our blood, but our pattern recognition range drops - especially with the reduced colors - making it hard to know what you're looking at until it's pretty close to you. Which means that vampires operating in wilderness nighttime darkness levels has to get pretty close to their prey to make an informed decision about whether to try or feed on them or not, while the prey has basically the same odds of noticing them coming as if it was day time, even if they wouldn't know why a human sized blob is approaching them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T04:36:07-07:00","id":1256687,"title":"","content":"Becuase they wanted night vision to be a protean 1 power wich is a same becuase they could have give you something cool.In requiem nigh vision is an standard power becuase the beast is a creature of the dark and protean theme is metmorphosis and the hability to steal natural adaptations from other predators.<br /> <br /> If you want to know more about protean in Requiem 2ED it was open devolopment so you can consult the discipline here<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1juI7Er1pUnl79v9zt8NCu4q6jynnCGKJvMZwHJHot7s/pub\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...MZwHJHot7s/pub</a><br /> <br /> The beuty and versatibility of the disciplines in VTR 2ED is something unseen in all the Vampire games from V5 to V1.They also were balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 09-23-2018, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T04:43:02-07:00","id":1256688,"title":"","content":"In the dark we have very low &quot;visual acuity&quot;. Our vision becomes a matter of casting a wide net searching for light and movement. Fine detail and colour are discarded, and shapes and movement become the primary focus.<br /> <br /> I think that seeing details in the dark should be much higher difficulty, but outside of pitch black situations it shouldn't inflict that much difficulty.<br /> <br /> Protean 1 and Serpentis 2, and Abyss Mysticism, can allow you to see much better (or even perfectly) in the dark. This removes difficulty hikes from pitch black situations, and removes difficulty spikes for seeing certain things like fine detail and colour when there isn't much light (although it depends on how you are &quot;seeing&quot;; the Setite method of flicking the air with their tongue won't reveal colour or fine details, it just gives them a sense of their surroundings, while Gangrel are able to see everything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T08:11:27-07:00","id":1256713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256672#post1256672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Setite and Lasombra seem like they should have some means of night vision...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak to Nosferatu, but one would assume they learn to navigate warrens and familiar crypts and underground passages, by touch and memory. They almost must by default, given how they prefer their lairs as labyrinthine and trap-laden as possible anyhow. Being able to do otherwise, in fact, through discipline use not innately available to Nossies makes warrens penetrable in ways they may not necessarily be able to expect, by my reckoning.<br /> <br /> Remember, out-of-clan disciplines are still available to vampires, they're just more difficult to learn. I've always ruled most Nosferatu (hell, most vampires) worth their salt learn Auspex one way or the other despite the difficulty, if for no reason other than expedience and convenience, and ancillae and elders should be expected to know it to some degree. Certainly, in a decent warren there will be at least one Nosferatu with education in Auspex, who due to the more harmonious than usual internal relations of the clan would be willing to teach it at a relative pittance in prestation debt.<br /> <br /> As far as the Lasombra and Setites, they already have means of night vision. Lasombra have the Darksight merit which can also be imparted via Abyss Mysticism; while it's not the most common thing, it still exists and I want to say one source book (the Revised clanbook?) makes the point while it's rare in the modern nights setting, it was a lot more common before the modern period for a myriad of reasons. Setites' Serpentis 2 power gives them enhanced sensitivity to taste and vibration, which allows them to navigate and act in darkness without necessarily being able to see.<br /> <br /> All the same, my ruling as an ST on the topic in general, is that since vampires no longer have metabolisms they don't have to transition to night vision as living humans do, and likewise they're not susceptible to disruption of night vision. By default, vampire vision isn't more acute than living human vision, but they can always see as well as they possibly could otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T08:30:06-07:00","id":1256718,"title":"","content":"Protean 1 would become pointless. LARP would become a rather dull experience and since Vampires are monsters of civilization, they are used to live in cities with some source of light available.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T11:50:20-07:00","id":1256773,"title":"","content":"Giving vampires night vision is one of my older house rules. I replace Protean level 1 with a different power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T12:22:34-07:00","id":1256781,"title":"","content":"V5 should have also given us plant ghouls, and a secret language of Kindred called &quot;the cacophony&quot; where they talk about Vampiric matters in plain sight. Ooh! And maybe &quot;feeding&quot; should be called &quot;the requiem&quot;- oh wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T12:41:18-07:00","id":1256783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256773#post1256773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving vampires night vision is one of my older house rules. I replace Protean level 1 with a different power.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you use?<br /> For some reason I got the idea of getting really hairy in my head. 1 level of natural armour, massive Masquerade breach as you look like bigfoot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T12:48:26-07:00","id":1256784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256773#post1256773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving vampires night vision is one of my older house rules. I replace Protean level 1 with a different power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What power do you replace it with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T13:32:48-07:00","id":1256787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256773#post1256773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving vampires night vision is one of my older house rules. I replace Protean level 1 with a different power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a neat idea.<br /> <br /> Poaching an idea from Trinity's shapeshifting Aptitude, Biokinesis, an alternate level 1 Protean power could allow the vampire to make minor changes to their body structure to specialize towards one type of activity, say increasing dice pools or effective Dexterity for swimming, climbing or running, so that a Gangrel might seem unnaturally good at getting around in the wild (able to run faster than her foes, or climb seemingly inaccessible cliffs, or swim like a fish).<br /> <br /> Thickening one's hide to give temporary extra soak would seem like a neat idea, for a clan that didn't already have Fortitude.<br /> <br /> Tying it into a pre-existing Vampire mechanic, the ability to spend blood to boost Strength, Dexterity or Stamina, could be another tack, and I'm fond of the idea of mechanics that tie together like that, and synergize. So a vampire with this alternate protean 1 might get an extra point to an Attribute raised, or the boost might last an additional turn (or, for non-combat uses, like boosting Dex and then running a long distance, or boosting Stamina to endure an inhospitable climate, or boosting Strength before building a barn or digging a tunnel, allow the 'boost' to last an entire scene!).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T15:52:51-07:00","id":1256818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256784#post1256784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What power do you replace it with?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eyrelliah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256783#post1256783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you use?<br /> For some reason I got the idea of getting really hairy in my head. 1 level of natural armour, massive Masquerade breach as you look like bigfoot...</div> </div> </div> </div>Spider climbing. It is an iconic vampire power that isn't represented with Disciplines, only an obscure Sabbat Thaumaturgy ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T03:23:00-07:00","id":1256921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256818#post1256818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spider climbing. It is an iconic vampire power that isn't represented with Disciplines, only an obscure Sabbat Thaumaturgy ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's sort of what the climbing bonus from the claws is supposed to represent. Without the climbing bonus, the claws are just an aggravated damage knife, which is a bit underwhelming in a chronicle where mortals are the primary antagonists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T04:38:43-07:00","id":1256929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatterofTact</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256921#post1256921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's sort of what the climbing bonus from the claws is supposed to represent. Without the climbing bonus, the claws are just an aggravated damage knife, which is a bit underwhelming in a chronicle where mortals are the primary antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, are you saying that being able to pop out razor sharp claws and rend people asunder is <i>underwhelming</i>? My sincere apologies, but you and I have very different ideas about the value of claws.<br /> <br /> Also, if I were to make Spider Climb the base Protean power, I would make it so the vampire doesn't even need to use their hands to do it. They can walk on walls and ceilings as easily as a mortal walks on the floor. Everything from <a href=\"https://youtu.be/o8_cxk0JOdM\" target=\"_blank\">Interview with the Vampire</a> to <a href=\"https://youtu.be/u22IeVke2fQ\" target=\"_blank\">Jojo's Bizarre Adventure</a> (although the last one is questionable, granted) has done that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T05:31:44-07:00","id":1256936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256929#post1256929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, are you saying that being able to pop out razor sharp claws and rend people asunder is <i>underwhelming</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I don't know how they work in Vampire 5, as I don't own it yet, but as I recall in 20th they are Strength +1 aggravated, which is really just Strength +1 lethal against mortals, which is just a knife that causes a masquerade breach at the cost of 1 blood point. So yes, the climbing bonus is an important bonus in my estimation.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that a fix to Protean 1 shouldn't accidentally cause other problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23590-matteroftact","name":"MatterofTact","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T07:34:57-07:00","id":1256955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256787#post1256787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Poaching an idea from Trinity's shapeshifting Aptitude, Biokinesis, an alternate level 1 Protean power could allow the vampire to make minor changes to their body structure to specialize towards one type of activity, say increasing dice pools or effective Dexterity for swimming, climbing or running, so that a Gangrel might seem unnaturally good at getting around in the wild (able to run faster than her foes, or climb seemingly inaccessible cliffs, or swim like a fish).</div> </div> </div> </div>Moving away from the debate over Eyes of the Beast per se, didn't Mariners have an alternate set of Protean powers in one of the older source books, that reflected their aquatic nature? I really, really want to say there was a variant to Eyes of the Beast that enhanced scent and taste to be like a shark's, instead of sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T09:19:45-07:00","id":1256970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256955#post1256955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moving away from the debate over Eyes of the Beast per se, didn't Mariners have an alternate set of Protean powers in one of the older source books, that reflected their aquatic nature? I really, really want to say there was a variant to Eyes of the Beast that enhanced scent and taste to be like a shark's, instead of sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dolphin's Unsight, from <i>Blood-Dimmed Tides</i> (p. 36), is the Mariner version of Protean 1, essentially trading night vision for sonar. It is, per the RAW, useless above water, though I could think of a few situations where it would make sense. Navigating dark tunnels or traveling without using vision (members of the Lightless Path of Night might be interested) come to mind. The Mariner version of Feral Claws is, next to Unsight, the most noticeably changed of the powers; Phocidaean Webbing grants strength+2 Aggravated attacks with the sharp webbing formed between the fingers, and triples swimming speed on top of negating any penalties involved in moving underwater.<br /> <br /> The climbing bonus given by claws is helpful, but I feel that it's always been meant to be limited, rather than subtle and freeform wall crawling. Oddly, one particular thing that climbing using Protean 2 has often reminded me of is how Gargoyles (of Disney fame) scaled solid stone by clawing into it. It's not exactly subtle, but I don't think it's meant to be. Protean, as a Discipline, is rarely subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-24-2018, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T10:09:33-07:00","id":1256976,"title":"","content":"&quot;Why didn't V5 make &quot;see in the dark&quot; standard for all vampires?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because the vampires of Masquerade are at the end of the dance, humans.<br /> Undead humans that acquire occult and mystical powers through the vampirism. But they stay basically humans. The animalistic features are (or were, I still don't know where V5 will go) a trait of the Protean Discipline.<br /> A Cainite is, at core and without its Discipline, a bloodsucking corpse with a Beast but without real occult powers beside channeling blood to boost its phisical traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T10:16:10-07:00","id":1256977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256976#post1256976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why didn't V5 make &quot;see in the dark&quot; standard for all vampires?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because the vampires of Masquerade are at the end of the dance, humans.<br /> Undead humans that acquire occult and mystical powers through the vampirism. But they stay basically humans. The animalistic features are (or were, I still don't know where V5 will go) a trait of the Protean Discipline.<br /> A Cainite is, at core and without its Discipline, a bloodsucking corpse with a Beast but without real occult powers beside channeling blood to boost its phisical traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why can't they boost their physical trait of &quot;eyes&quot; with some negligible amount of blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T10:19:58-07:00","id":1256979,"title":"","content":"because becoming stronger or swifter or sturdier is a human trait that gets enhanced<br /> &quot;seeing in the dark&quot;, the old and dear &quot;<i>Darkvision</i>&quot; of D&amp;D, is something you achieve when your pupils change shape, resembling the ones of nocturnal animals, it's not a boost, it's shapeshifting<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T10:49:03-07:00","id":1256983,"title":"","content":"Probably didn't feel a need to as it wasn't that way in prior editions. Honestly, the aspect is pretty negligible given it is very easily hand waved.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256979#post1256979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because becoming stronger or swifter or sturdier is a human trait that gets enhanced<br /> &quot;seeing in the dark&quot;, the old and dear &quot;<i>Darkvision</i>&quot; of D&amp;D, is something you achieve when your pupils change shape, resembling the ones of nocturnal animals, it's not a boost, it's shapeshifting</div> </div> </div> </div> This feels really pedantic. At the end of the day, Kindred are mystical creatures. What they achieve through the blood is, at the very least, achieved through that. If someone wanted to ascribe an aspect to that, seems fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 09-24-2018, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T10:49:20-07:00","id":1256984,"title":"","content":"In V5 you essentially can do this, as a Blood Surge can apply to a dice pool that includes any Attribute which implies that Kindred can enhance any of their core stats with Vitae now - and since all the examples I see for perception based activities seem to use Wits + Awareness/Insight/Investigation/etc I would see it as being viable to Blood Surge to get a bonus to a perception based task. So, it is kind of like this in V5:<br /> <br /> Blood Surge: Rouse Check, Bonus Dice based on Blood Potency, does not negate &quot;darkness&quot; issues (though may offset penalty)<br /> Auspex: No Rouse, Bonus Dice based on Auspex, prone to sensory overload, does not negate &quot;darkness&quot; issues (though may offset penalty)<br /> Protean: No Rouse, No Bonus Dice, gain Intimidation Bonus, negates penalties from &quot;darkness&quot; including supernatural<br /> <br /> So, really, Blood Surge and Auspex are a compensation for a handicap, while Protean is altering the eyes to remove a handicap entirely. At least that is the V5 approach to it. Previous Editions I think are pretty similar, though enhancing Attributes with Blood was relegated to the Physical category so you would lose that off the options list and only have Disciplines to rely on. Long story short, WW basically did give all Kindred &quot;see in the dark&quot; in V5, it just comes with a risk of Hunger unless you have a dedicated power for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">-Red</span></b> V5 Fan Content: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1259556-v5-the-masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">The Masquerade</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256114-v5-tzimisce-and-vicissitude\" target=\"_blank\">Tzimisce and Vicissitude</a> (non Program take), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1253331-loresheets-chicago\" target=\"_blank\">Loresheet: Chicago</a> (pre CbN V5), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1251576-v5-resonance-flavor\" target=\"_blank\">Resonance Flavor</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1291918-v5-morality\" target=\"_blank\">Morality System</a> Project Manager, Developer, Community Outreach at <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Entertainment</a>","edited":{"userid":6164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6164-red-eye","user":"Red Eye","date":". 09-24-2018, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6164-red-eye","name":"Red Eye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6164_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T11:14:22-07:00","id":1256993,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24483_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24483\" data-vbnamecard=\"24483\">SalamanDer</a> <br /> Except, as noted above, humans aren't blind in anything but the most absolute darkness. And we have other senses besides sight as it is (we're just very visually oriented and take training to make better use of our other senses actively). If a vampire's blood alone can be channeled to let them perform superhuman feats of strength (and do so without the physical changes necessary to comport with physics), the idea that they can't increase their sight especially (as blood flow and muscle control are really important to sight) doesn't really hold a lot of water. You don't need to shapeshift to see better.<br /> <br /> VtM vampires also have plenty of innate powers that buck they idea that they're just &quot;undead humans.&quot; Humans don't have the ability to staunch wounds reflexively, retractable fangs, or wound closing saliva for other examples.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e is, again, a great example here. Vampires in VtR 2e don't get &quot;Darkvision,&quot; just reduced penalties from darkness for general sight based perception. Except for a key thematic thing: blood. When it comes to blood (and heartbeats) VtR 2e vampires get huge perception boosts. This also means the classic &quot;vampire can feel the blood in your veins and fresh vampires can get disoriented by all the blood pumping around them&quot; trope actually works. VtR 2e's Auspex and Protean work just fine without specific &quot;see in the dark&quot; powers. Protean (as linked above as well) in particular lets you shapeshift to far more potent sensory improvements than seeing in the dark (such as bat level echolocation, or a snake's infrared vision, etc.) with are useful for more than explaining how vampires hunted for human blood without Protean 1 and before modern cities in VtM.<br /> <br /> Though Blood Surge written more openly does at least partially address the OP even if didn't see it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-24-2018, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T12:41:59-07:00","id":1257006,"title":"","content":"I'm perfectly fine with vampires not having any special bonus to see in the dark by default. There's two level 1 disciplines that help with that already. In fact, if you look at vampire fiction as a whole, the most recurring power that vampires have is super strength and not all vampires in this game have Potence either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T13:10:01-07:00","id":1257010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256993#post1256993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24483_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24483\" data-vbnamecard=\"24483\">SalamanDer</a><br /> VtR 2e is, again, a great example here. Vampires in VtR 2e don't get &quot;Darkvision,&quot; just reduced penalties from darkness for general sight based perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which page was that on? We have been playing 2e for some time now and I seemed to have missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T14:09:07-07:00","id":1257021,"title":"","content":"Page 90-91 under the Kindred Senses heading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T14:32:37-07:00","id":1257031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257006#post1257006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm perfectly fine with vampires not having any special bonus to see in the dark by default. There's two level 1 disciplines that help with that already. In fact, if you look at vampire fiction as a whole, the most recurring power that vampires have is super strength and not all vampires in this game have Potence either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that most cinematic vampires seem to start with 1 dot of Potence, Celerity, Fortitude and Auspex, and then it's a crap shoot whether or not they will learn other stuff (like Dominate or Protean).<br /> <br /> That might be an interesting variation on the game, for every starting vampire to have a dot in those 4 Disciplines, and then 1 or 2 dots to put into Clan Disciplines. Clan Disciplines and Out of Clan Disciplines would remain the same, so that a Toreador would have to pay OOC costs to raise Potence or Fortitude to 2. Like vampires from Blade or Buffy or Anne Rice novels or whatever, even a 'newbie' vampire would gain some strength, speed and resilience (and enhanced senses). Starting vampires would be a bit tougher than currently, but that's fine, they'd still be complete pushovers compared to Garou, and the 'lore' generally portrays *all* vampires as at least somewhat stronger/faster/tougher than the average human.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T14:38:55-07:00","id":1257034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KarlB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257006#post1257006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm perfectly fine with vampires not having any special bonus to see in the dark by default. There's two level 1 disciplines that help with that already. In fact, if you look at vampire fiction as a whole, the most recurring power that vampires have is super strength and not all vampires in this game have Potence either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean is among the &quot;clan secret&quot; disciplines (even though it's still the most commonly available one) and it's debateable whether Auspex really imparts night vision, especially at level 1 without having bought more levels.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, yeah, vampires in fiction often have supernatural strength and speed - which is <i>exactly</i> why blood pumping exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T14:43:55-07:00","id":1257035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257021#post1257021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 90-91 under the Kindred Senses heading.</div> </div> </div> </div>found the disconnect. you said VtR I read VtM. and I was like I've never seen that in 2e and we play that every other week. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T15:28:25-07:00","id":1257049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256781#post1256781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 should have also given us plant ghouls, and a secret language of Kindred called &quot;the cacophony&quot; where they talk about Vampiric matters in plain sight. Ooh! And maybe &quot;feeding&quot; should be called &quot;the requiem&quot;- oh wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, hahah, hahahahahahahahahahahahahahahaaaaaaa! Great!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T15:33:32-07:00","id":1257052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256977#post1256977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why can't they boost their physical trait of &quot;eyes&quot; with some negligible amount of blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is in fact mentiond in the story at the beginning of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T17:50:10-07:00","id":1257057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256983#post1256983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels really pedantic. At the end of the day, Kindred are mystical creatures. What they achieve through the blood is, at the very least, achieved through that. If someone wanted to ascribe an aspect to that, seems fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may be mystical, in some ways, but they are still the more mundane of the supernatural denizens of the World of Darkness.<br /> But my point is more on &quot;a vampire without Disciplines is still more or less a human&quot;, they can mostly do what humans do (unlike werewolves, for example, you take Gifts out of a Garou and you still have a Garou). Disciplines are what give them the supernatural edge they have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256993#post1256993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24483_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24483\" data-vbnamecard=\"24483\">SalamanDer</a><br /> Except, as noted above, humans aren't blind in anything but the most absolute darkness. And we have other senses besides sight as it is (we're just very visually oriented and take training to make better use of our other senses actively). If a vampire's blood alone can be channeled to let them perform superhuman feats of strength (and do so without the physical changes necessary to comport with physics), the idea that they can't increase their sight especially (as blood flow and muscle control are really important to sight) doesn't really hold a lot of water. You don't need to shapeshift to see better.<br /> <br /> VtM vampires also have plenty of innate powers that buck they idea that they're just &quot;undead humans.&quot; Humans don't have the ability to staunch wounds reflexively, retractable fangs, or wound closing saliva for other examples.<br /> <br /> VtR 2e is, again, a great example here. Vampires in VtR 2e don't get &quot;Darkvision,&quot; just reduced penalties from darkness for general sight based perception. Except for a key thematic thing: blood. When it comes to blood (and heartbeats) VtR 2e vampires get huge perception boosts. This also means the classic &quot;vampire can feel the blood in your veins and fresh vampires can get disoriented by all the blood pumping around them&quot; trope actually works. VtR 2e's Auspex and Protean work just fine without specific &quot;see in the dark&quot; powers. Protean (as linked above as well) in particular lets you shapeshift to far more potent sensory improvements than seeing in the dark (such as bat level echolocation, or a snake's infrared vision, etc.) with are useful for more than explaining how vampires hunted for human blood without Protean 1 and before modern cities in VtM.<br /> <br /> Though Blood Surge written more openly does at least partially address the OP even if didn't see it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I get for oversemplificating.<br /> <br /> Human's are not blind in darkness, and that's a thing. This doesn't mean they can see well in the darkness. And this doesn't mean even that Auspex 1 and Protean 1 are equivalent. One let you see better, so it can lessen the malus in poor lighting, the other let you see in ambients were the human eye could not distinguish almost anything like they are in broad light. There's a large difference.<br /> Now, if we're speaking of Heightened Senses (Sight) is a matter, if we talk about Eyes of the Beast is a whole another matter, and I think here we are mistaking the two effects. Because the example you're making of is from the Auspex area, but &quot;see in the dark&quot; (original question of the topic) is domain of Protean 1.<br /> So you don't need to shapeshift to see better. Totally true. But you need to shapeshift to see in the darkest night like it's all well illuminated.<br /> <br /> Moving on, as I mentioned above, Cainites are still extremely humans. While anyone can detail the structural difference with a human (they also burn like crisps), they are not able to do any of the astonishing feats usually associated to vampires. Yes, they sprout fangs, they can patch themselves up, close with saliva wounds they inflicted biting their prey (I don't think they can randomly close wounds like some wannabe miracle-worker) and can boost their body almost as they had a huge adrenaline surge. But any of this can give them the supernatural edge they have?<br /> I think no. Without counting the obvious phisical differences, their actions without Disciplines, are all in the domain of a human. These are the Vampires of Masquerade (and, by the way, this is why the &quot;withering&quot; is so fearsome, without Disciplines even the fearsome Elders and Methusealk get kicked down to &quot;human level&quot;).<br /> And, I repeat, I was stating it like this in response to the question of the topic.<br /> <br /> I don't know how the Vampires of Requiem are, but the ones of Masquerade are just humans knocked out of the mundane world with very little natural abilities. Beside those, they have the Disciplines, and the Disciplines are the bulk of a vampire's power. And they get the Beast too, as a wrapping to the whole package. Giving more supernatural skill to the vampires would make them less &quot;masquerade&quot;. As a I see it, that's the core concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":24483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","user":"SalamanDer","date":". 09-24-2018, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T18:57:38-07:00","id":1257062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257057#post1257057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They may be mystical, in some ways, but they are still the more mundane of the supernatural denizens of the World of Darkness.<br /> But my point is more on &quot;a vampire without Disciplines is still more or less a human&quot;, they can mostly do what humans do (unlike werewolves, for example, you take Gifts out of a Garou and you still have a Garou). Disciplines are what give them the supernatural edge they have.</div> </div> </div> </div> And my point is that 'more or less human' doesn't matter. Whether or not they are 'more or less human', they are ultimately <i>not </i>human. <i>Ultimately </i>they are mystical/supernatural entities, so saying 'sure, they also have night vision' seems fine. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T19:06:58-07:00","id":1257063,"title":"","content":"Vampires have all sorts of crazy powerful natural abilities outside of Disciplines. The blood bound is likely the most powerful ability that vampires have. They can also regenerate damage, grow fangs, have the kiss to induce pleasure in their prey, and the ability to heal bite wounds with a kiss. Those are all overt supernatural abilities. Seeing in the dark is something that a human can do with a piece of modern equipment. It's something that plenty of animals can do, depending on how you define it. It would be one of the least noteworthy supernatural abilities that come with being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T01:12:45-07:00","id":1257116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257034#post1257034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...and it's debateable whether Auspex really imparts night vision, especially at level 1 without having bought more levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. At least not in V5 (and I seem to recall it was clearly stated at least in Revised as well but I do not have those books on hand).<br /> <br /> From V5 page 249 (in the pdf), Auspex 'Heightened Senses': <i>The vampire\u2019s senses sharpen to a preternatural degree, giving them the ability to see in pitch darkness, hear ultrasonic frequencies and smell the fear of cowering prey.</i><br /> <br /> Plain and upfront, use Auspex 1 'Heightened Senses' and you got both darkvision and actually sonar as well it seems.<br /> <br /> Cog.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/489-cogitare","name":"cogitare","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T02:12:11-07:00","id":1257134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cogitare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257116#post1257116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not. At least not in V5 (and I seem to recall it was clearly stated at least in Revised as well but I do not have those books on hand).<br /> <br /> From V5 page 249 (in the pdf), Auspex 'Heightened Senses': <i>The vampire\u2019s senses sharpen to a preternatural degree, giving them the ability to see in pitch darkness, hear ultrasonic frequencies and smell the fear of cowering prey.</i><br /> <br /> Plain and upfront, use Auspex 1 'Heightened Senses' and you got both darkvision and actually sonar as well it seems.<br /> <br /> Cog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. V20 explicitly mentions that Auspex 1 does *not* grant night vision (but halves the penalties due to other senses making up for it). VRev used the same text.<br /> Of course, the question remains if V5 Auspex completely negates the penalty for darkness or if you can simply use your bonus dice to make up for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T02:49:13-07:00","id":1257136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257134#post1257134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the question remains if V5 Auspex completely negates the penalty for darkness or if you can simply use your bonus dice to make up for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T05:47:38-07:00","id":1257175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257062#post1257062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And my point is that 'more or less human' doesn't matter. Whether or not they are 'more or less human', they are ultimately <i>not </i>human. <i>Ultimately </i>they are mystical/supernatural entities, so saying 'sure, they also have night vision' seems fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, seems fine.<br /> Unless the fact that, without Disciplines, they have supernatural edges but are mostly humans.<br /> Which they are, and therefore they don't have night vision.<br /> <br /> But I would prefer to not continue too much with a fruitless discussion, as it's like two pages that it's a wall against wall confrontation and all boils down to if you prefer VtR approach or VtM's one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T06:20:30-07:00","id":1257181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257175#post1257175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, seems fine.<br /> Unless the fact that, without Disciplines, they have supernatural edges but are mostly humans.<br /> Which they are, and therefore they don't have night vision.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your insistence on using the word mostly just keeps proving my point, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I would prefer to not continue too much with a fruitless discussion, as it's like two pages that it's a wall against wall confrontation and all boils down to if you prefer VtR approach or VtM's one. </div> </div> </div> Which also just supports my point. I'm not the one trying to appeal to a sense of what Kindred are as a restriction, just that it boils down to one's preference.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 09-25-2018, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T09:48:12-07:00","id":1257212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257181#post1257181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your insistence on using the word mostly just keeps proving my point, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may also be mostly (ok, I'll stop <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) because those are assuptions, not things carved in the rock, so I prefer to use a terminology of probability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257181#post1257181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which also just supports my point. I'm not the one trying to appeal to a sense of what Kindred are as a restriction, just that it boils down to one's preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I was just stating a possible reason why the aforementioned power was never included in the base traits of Masquerade's Kindred.<br /> I'm happy we're on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T13:10:28-07:00","id":1257251,"title":"","content":"I houserule that vampires can see in the dark, simply because I find the idea of vampires stumbling about in a victim's bedroom like the &quot;Dead, and Loving It!&quot; version of Dracula to be completely preposterous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T13:40:28-07:00","id":1257256,"title":"","content":"sounds good, are you replacing Protean 1 with another power? I would like to see a write up if you do one. Having more choices is cool to me and I might add it to my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T06:36:42-07:00","id":1257351,"title":"","content":"While Im personally not a fan of universal night vision, a few easy and quick changes could be that all Cainites have the Eyes if the Beast ability, including the glowing eyes portion, while Protean 1 allows night vision with or without glowing eyes, and does allow partial vision through Obtenebration that neither Cainite sight or Auspex do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T06:41:38-07:00","id":1257352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257351#post1257351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Im personally not a fan of universal night vision, a few easy and quick changes could be that all Cainites have the Eyes if the Beast ability, including the glowing eyes portion, while Protean 1 allows night vision with or without glowing eyes, and does allow partial vision through Obtenebration that neither Cainite sight or Auspex do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, V5 Eyes of the Beast seems to include piercing Obtenebration: &quot;While active, the user ignores any sight penalties imposed by darkness, including supernatural&quot;. We'll see whether Obtenebration is somehow written to supercede this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T07:30:01-07:00","id":1257360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257352#post1257352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, V5 Eyes of the Beast seems to include piercing Obtenebration: &quot;While active, the user ignores any sight penalties imposed by darkness, including supernatural&quot;. We'll see whether Obtenebration is somehow written to supercede this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the book include any examples of supernatural darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T08:13:34-07:00","id":1257370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257360#post1257360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the book include any examples of supernatural darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense of the Sacred Haven comes to mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T08:37:51-07:00","id":1257373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257352#post1257352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, V5 Eyes of the Beast seems to include piercing Obtenebration: &amp;quot;While active, the user ignores any sight penalties imposed by darkness, including supernatural&amp;quot;. We'll see whether Obtenebration is somehow written to supercede this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prior editions of Obtenebration's Shroud of Night indicate it is not Supernatural Darkness (in the D&amp;D sense), but rather a partially tangible oily cloud, similar to walking through water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T14:02:47-07:00","id":1257441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257212#post1257212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I was just stating a possible reason why the aforementioned power was never included in the base traits of Masquerade's Kindred.<br /> I'm happy we're on the same page.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't the worst theory, given the original poster's question could be read as, &quot;Why, in-universe, do vampires not have night vision?&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampires have long been said to have the same form they possessed at the moment of the embrace. This stasis, presumably, includes the ratio of rods to cones in the eye, the resting size of the pupil, and so forth. It makes sense, all else being the same, that night vision would not be enhanced. So, if you are running a game and don't want enhanced night-vision there is a rationale for it.<br /> <br /> That said, how many vampires need glasses, in canon? How many vampires are described as spending eternity with a pimple just about to pop, or eternal bad-breath because they were embraced a few hours after a nice big dinner of pasta and garlic bread? How many were embraced the night before an appointment at the salon, and spend eternity with grey roots? Given most embraces occur in the dead of night, why don't most male vampires have 20-plus hours of stubble on their face?<br /> <br /> I've long assumed that while it's RAW true that vampires are a perfect snapshot of the moment of the embrace, there is a subtle process of improvement taking place. If for no other reason than why don't more vampires have the open wound flaw from the draining part of the embrace? So, skin gets a little clearer, tummies a little flatter, hair a little silkier, and, yes, eyes see a little bit better. I assume most fledglings move slightly toward their ego ideal, reducing minor flaws and increasing their best attributes. The process sometimes goes wrong, like with Polonius' sunburn, or more horrifically for the Nosferatu, but mostly it's reliable and subtle. (Vicissitude might, then, be read as an intense amplification of this process.)<br /> <br /> This process means if you want to enhance night vision, go ahead, you have a rationale for this, too.<br /> <br /> So, it comes down to a balance being struck between maintaining internal consistency of the details of vampiric existence, and the authorial license to smooth off the details to make a more pleasant story.<br /> <br /> NB: Personally, I do not grant free night-vision. Players can buy Protean. Otherwise, vampires being afraid of the dark is a feature, not a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T14:06:27-07:00","id":1257442,"title":"","content":"Kindred Senses.This is Requiem 2ED giving all vampires standard nigh vision plus enchanced blood smell and the hability to hear the hearthbeats if they are close enough like the predators they are.<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/seeing-in-the-dark/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/seeing-in-the-dark/</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T14:14:24-07:00","id":1257443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257441#post1257441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, how many vampires need glasses, in canon? How many vampires are described as spending eternity with a pimple just about to pop, or eternal bad-breath because they were embraced a few hours after a nice big dinner of pasta and garlic bread? How many were embraced the night before an appointment at the salon, and spend eternity with grey roots? Given most embraces occur in the dead of night, why don't most male vampires have 20-plus hours of stubble on their face?<br /> <br /> I've long assumed that while it's RAW true that vampires are a perfect snapshot of the moment of the embrace, there is a subtle process of improvement taking place.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already canon, by the way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T15:14:44-07:00","id":1257454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257443#post1257443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's already canon, by the way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah? Hmm. It's been so many years, I guess I forget what's a houserule and what's canon. Things like having immortal stubble or an eternal papercut rarely comes up in play, so I mostly handwave it. Do you have the reference, so I can read the details?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T17:49:30-07:00","id":1257474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257454#post1257454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah? Hmm. It's been so many years, I guess I forget what's a houserule and what's canon. Things like having immortal stubble or an eternal papercut rarely comes up in play, so I mostly handwave it. Do you have the reference, so I can read the details?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire Revised, page 33, third paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T09:03:34-07:00","id":1303962,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that if players and Storytellers think it's too difficult for the characters to do anything without being able to see in the dark, you just lack either problem-solving skills, creativity, or imagination.<br /> <br /> Here is a question for everyone. <i>In real life, how often do you 'have difficulty' functioning at night due to darkness?</i><br /> <br /> You probably don't. Light is abundant. So the issue is moot. The problem only arises when you WANT it to be dark because you're hunting or something. Just be stealthy. You don't need a POWER for that. Unless you need to guarantee you aren't seen, then there is Obfuscate. But I see seeing in the dark as totally unnecessary for night-to-night living for a vampire.<br /> <br /> Seeing in the dark is just not <i>necessary</i>.<br /> <br /> Why did the writers not include it in V5? Because more than some of you realize, that would turn a lot of the fundamentals of vampires on it's head, moving away from what they have always been. It would cause lots of unintended consequences. They also recognize it's not necessary as things work out just fine the way they are.<br /> <br /> In another thread, I used this argument against vampires seeing in the dark naturally. <b>Vampires are cursed humans.</b> They aren't cursed and then <i>given gifts afterward to compensate. </i>No, that would be like sending someone to prison for murder and then instead of putting him in a cell, you give him an entire country to roam around in because otherwise it would be too cruel. What the hell kind of punishment/curse would that be? I say Vampires are cursed. It comes with some bad stuff. Makes life difficult. Deal with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1257441#post1257441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">vampires being afraid of the dark is a feature, not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13189,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","user":"Knowledgeseeker","date":". 04-10-2019, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T09:25:46-07:00","id":1303970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1303962#post1303962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the opinion that if players and Storytellers think it's too difficult for the characters to do anything without being able to see in the dark, you just lack either problem-solving skills, creativity, or imagination.<br /> <br /> Here is a question for everyone. <i>In real life, how often do you 'have difficulty' functioning at night due to darkness?</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of times. That's why you buy flashligths and candles for when ligth goes off. Perhaps it's becuase I live in a city where blackouts happen a lot, but I function pretty bad w/o sources of ilumination and consider flashlights and such a rather convinient thing to have at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You probably don't. Light is abundant. So the issue is moot. The problem only arises when you WANT it to be dark because you're hunting or something. So you want it to be dark. Now you want to be able to see in the darkness. Well why don't you just sneak up on them and be stealthy instead of being able to see in the darkness?<br /> <br /> Seeing in the dark is just not <i>necessary</i>. </div> </div> </div>And the whole point here it's that vampires skulking with flashlights and candles it's anticlimatic, not that it's necessary. It's just silly to play a night predator that has problems seeing at night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why did the writers not include it in V5? Because more than some of you realize, that would turn a lot of the fundamentals of vampires on it's head, moving away from what they have always been. It would cause lots of unintended consequences. They also recognize it's not necessary as things work out just fine the way they are. </div> </div> </div>No, they don't recognize it as necessary because nobody plays with &quot;vampires should have problems seeing at night&quot; in mind. No ST that I have known uses penalties for being in a dim lit area at night w/o a lantern. ST's just have their vampires move like it was day regardless if they are in New York or Dark Ages Transilvania. Do you make your vampires suffer a penalty in DA: Vampire when the sky it's clouded?, do they find harder to recognize people at distance than when playing another game in day-light?, have you EVER played with the fact that vampires live at night and can't see well in the dark, or it's night just a thematically colored day?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In another thread, I used this argument against vampires seeing in the dark naturally. Vampires are cursed humans. <b>They aren't cursed and then <i>given gifts afterward to compensate. </i></b>No, that would be like sending someone to prison for murder and then instead of putting him in a cell, you give him an entire country to roam around in because otherwise it would be too cruel. What the hell kind of punishment/curse would that be? I say Vampires are cursed. It comes with some bad stuff. Makes life difficult. Deal with it. </div> </div> </div>Yes they are. How do you call being immortal, unaging, immune to most diseases, capable of making yourself stronger, faster and more resistant in an instant, being able to get magical powers (Disciplines), heal most wounds, and enslave people to your blood? How does that makes your life more difficult?. WoD Vampires have a lot of problems, but they also have a lot of powers humans don't get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-10-2019, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T09:43:34-07:00","id":1303976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1303962#post1303962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a question for everyone. <i>In real life, how often do you 'have difficulty' functioning at night due to darkness?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Why do you think that in previous ages, the day of most people ended at sundown? Was Caine cursed post-1800 when major cities developed street lamps? The light pollution of the modern era is an exception, not a universal constant throughout human history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1303962#post1303962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably don't. Light is abundant. So the issue is moot. The problem only arises when you WANT it to be dark because you're hunting or something. Just be stealthy. You don't need a POWER for that. Unless you need to guarantee you aren't seen, then there is Obfuscate. But I see seeing in the dark as totally unnecessary for night-to-night living for a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do the Nosferatu warrens of your games look like? Do Nosferatu carry lamps with them when they venture through the sewers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1303962#post1303962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did the writers not include it in V5? Because more than some of you realize, that would turn a lot of the fundamentals of vampires on it's head, moving away from what they have always been. It would cause lots of unintended consequences. They also recognize it's not necessary as things work out just fine the way they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>What unintended consequences? What fundamentals of vampires? Right now, being able to see in the dark is a level 1 ability of two disciplines (two-and-a-half if you count Auspex). This is how &quot;fundamental&quot; it is that vampires must never get to see in darkness. And before you try to turn this around: No, it doesn't mean everyone should just go get the disciplines - gaining a discipline out of clan should be a reasonably big development for a character, not something that is necessary for any nocturnal predator.<br /> The idea that all vampires should never have darkvision - except for those five clans who get it for next to nothing - seems just ludicrous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1303962#post1303962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In another thread, I used this argument against vampires seeing in the dark naturally. <b>Vampires are cursed humans.</b> They aren't cursed and then <i>given gifts afterward to compensate. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>So I assume you play without disciplines, blood surges, blood bonds, halved damage for nearly all mundane weapons, extremely short healing times and probably half a dozen other abilities that make the &quot;cursed&quot; vampires obviously superhuman? Or is it just darkvision that would break the &quot;cursed&quot; aspect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T12:19:55-07:00","id":1304005,"title":"","content":"I kind of like that Vampires don't see naturally better in darkness than normal humans do. For the reasons that Vampires are supernaturally cursed people and not the results of millions of years of evolution, or at least in my games that's how it goes. And as mentioned it isn't very difficult to get hold of supernatural means of seeing in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T13:40:00-07:00","id":1304016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1303970#post1303970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the whole point here it's that vampires skulking with flashlights and candles it's anticlimatic, not that it's necessary. It's just silly to play a night predator that has problems seeing at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there is too much darkness in your chronicle that you need powers to see in the dark, hopefully that is intentional design by your Storyteller for the mood he's trying to create, otherwise he's just doing a bad job and punishing you for not being able to see in the dark. And you should get a different storyteller.<br /> <br /> According to Vampire lore, it seems likely that vampires received disciplines after the curse, NOT because of it. If this is the case, the 'Curse of Caine' is fitting as it banishes you to darkness in a world where there is only torchlight to see by which you are terrified of. And your fellow man who might keep you compay in this new dark world? You eat him. Eternally banished to walk the earth in darkness and eat people, and to be afraid of the only light source you are able to use... THAT is a punishment. That is a Dark Ages kind of damnation. And to top it all off, you're hungry. The hunger never ends. So no, I don't think that anything compensates for the curse. With the disciplines coming after the curse, being given by another source, the point of the curse was just that. To curse. God gave no compensation or mercy.<br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm not arguing for players to be punished while in the dark. My point seems to be missed. I'm just arguing why the it seems logical that the curse of Caine would exclude vampires from being able to naturally see in the dark. I'm rationalizing here BECAUSE vampires CAN'T see in the dark naturally. My arguments stem from being able to strategically use darkness in storytelling for mood, and for lore and role play reasons. Makes sense to me. Maybe it does't make sense to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:00:35-07:00","id":1304021,"title":"","content":"Humans have been able to operate at night pretty well ever since fire was &quot;tamed&quot;. Maybe the day's toil in the field ended when the sun went down, but once you could light a hut with a flame, you could keep doing things. As other people have said, you can move about and travel at night pretty easily without an artificial light source. Maybe human eyes are not specialised to cope with low light, but they can. They may not be great for hunting animals at night but hunting other people is perfectly achievable.<br /> <br /> If you can't cope with moving about in a darkened house slowly and steathily, that's a personal failing. Let your eyes adjust and move slowly, most people can do it if they actually try.<br /> <br /> As for nosferatu, i've always pictured them having lights down there. The pitch dark entrance to the warren is part of what puts people off coming down. I don't think they actually live in the shit and piss, they most likely have a dry comfortable haven somewhere down there.<br /> <br /> This peculiar nightsight thing seems to be one of the more &quot;Vampions&quot; issues that i have seen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24824-notempathic","name":"NotEmpathic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:04:53-07:00","id":1304022,"title":"","content":"The &quot;vampires are cursed&quot; argument doesn't really work because it's being applied completely inconsistently as convenient. If you apply the concept consistently, dozens of other elements of the game would need to change. At the moment there is no functional difference between saying, &quot;Vampires shouldn't get any alleviation from darkness penalties because CURSE!&quot; and, &quot;I need to manufacture a reason to yell at people for being WRONG AND HORRIBLE on the Internet.&quot;<br /> <br /> If it isn't difficult to get access to supernatural senses? Well it can't be that important to the curse the game presents. It doesn't matter when Disciplines came into the picture. It doesn't matter if vampires are actually just evolved magical creatures or actually came from the Biblical Cain who got cursed by the Lord.<br /> <br /> Trying to rationalize defenses of the status quo just to defend the status quo is... pointless and borderline insulting.<br /> <br /> And finally? Read the Bible. Cain complains his original punishment was too harsh, and was shown mercy; the Mark of Cain is a sign of protection to keep Cain safe from other people that would kill him for his crime while he's already being punished by divine mandate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:06:38-07:00","id":1304024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NotEmpathic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304021#post1304021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This peculiar nightsight thing seems to be one of the more &quot;Vampions&quot; issues that i have seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or we saw how VtR 2e handled Kindred senses, thought it was awesome, and are baffled by V5 not taking that from VtR 2e with all the other stuff V5 took from there as it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:20:48-07:00","id":1304027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304024#post1304024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or we saw how VtR 2e handled Kindred senses, thought it was awesome, and are baffled by V5 not taking that from VtR 2e with all the other stuff V5 took from there as it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe one more thing and they'd offically tip over into a VtR game.<br /> <br /> The more distance between the gamelines the better, others may like it but i'd prefer VtM to stay as much out of VtR as it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T14:45:17-07:00","id":1304031,"title":"","content":"As noted already though, in VtM Lore, this was a thing in pre-V5 books, it just never had mechanics. It's not like Touchstones that are a completely new thing to add to V5 because they were never a thing at all in VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T15:39:58-07:00","id":1304036,"title":"","content":"It just seems to be a fairly personal thing. From what you described of the VtR blood senses, the only time i can recall seeing that represented in a similar way was &quot;Dracula Untold&quot;.<br /> <br /> My characters in modern nights just always carry a torch, with a red filter lens if they're fancy. I generally play a Gangrel in Dark ages, so it's not a problem for them obviously, and the Gleam from my eyes lets the auspex users have a small amount of light to highten their sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T16:06:09-07:00","id":1304039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304036#post1304036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just seems to be a fairly personal thing. From what you described of the VtR blood senses, the only time i can recall seeing that represented in a similar way was &quot;Dracula Untold&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you recall other vampire myths where the vampire isn't capable of basically ignoring darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T16:36:09-07:00","id":1304041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304039#post1304039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you recall other vampire myths where the vampire isn't capable of basically ignoring darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you mean poor lighting or pitch darkness? Because whenever i generally think of any vampire from myth, whether baobhan sith, ustrel, penanggalan or the basic Hammer Horror Dracula, i don't go &quot;Can see in pitch darkness&quot;.<br /> <br /> Dim or gloomy light, yes, but never have i put &quot;darkvision&quot; on the list of vampiric standard ablities in my head...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T16:57:02-07:00","id":1304045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304036#post1304036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just seems to be a fairly personal thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a disagreement? It's kind of bound to be 'personal.'<br /> <br /> What I find most frustrating with it though, is the 'anti-senses' side are basically twisting themselves in knots to try to make their argument something more than, &quot;VtM never had mechanics for this, so it shouldn't have mechanics now,&quot; because everything comes back to that. Lore? The lore of the game actually says vampires should have limited bonus to senses but there weren't mechanics for it beyond it being available through a few Disciplines that a decent number of Clans have ready access too. The 'mood' argument is undermined by the 'practical' argument that light is easy enough to get, which means there's no mood highlighted by forcing vampires to be normal in the face of darkness. The mythology argument doesn't have anything that makes it important for a satirical juxtaposition that creatures of the night are kinda crappy nighttime predators without extra tools (mystic or mundane).<br /> <br /> You can like or dislike the state of things as a personal taste. But the attempts to look at the strength of the arguments for each side beyond taste is a lot more weighted in one direction; so just saying it's really just personal doesn't accomplish much besides seeming dismissive of one side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what you described of the VtR blood senses, the only time i can recall seeing that represented in a similar way was &quot;Dracula Untold&quot;. </div> </div> </div>OK... I can think of plenty of examples. VtR 2e's 'blood' senses apply beyond sight. Earlier depictions (esp. in text) rely more on hearing or smell than vision for these things both for the medium, and probably thematic concerns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My characters in modern nights just always carry a torch, with a red filter lens if they're fancy. I generally play a Gangrel in Dark ages, so it's not a problem for them obviously, and the Gleam from my eyes lets the auspex users have a small amount of light to highten their sight. </div> </div> </div>So... what would it really matter if vampires had some basic bonuses to their senses that made the dark easier to navigate on some level?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304041#post1304041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean poor lighting or pitch darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to speak for Cifer, but the people generally arguing for increased vision bonuses mean poor lighting.<br /> <br /> For Cifer's example though, you really have to stretch to find vampires actively hindered by pitch black conditions. Which of those myths you cited actually have that as a thing that happens? In the vast majority of stories darkness is just skipped over. You don't go &quot;can see in pitch darkness&quot; because it's not actively highlighted, but the internal logic of the stories generally necessitate some level of boosted senses for the vampires to act the way they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dim or gloomy light, yes,... </div> </div> </div>Just remember, that's what a lot of us are basically saying the game should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T17:24:51-07:00","id":1304049,"title":"","content":"It's the dim/pitch thing that seems to be the breaking point. A lot of people, myself included, don't really think dim light is as big of an issue as other people. As you say, it's just not something that's generally highlighted. As with the Revised write up, it says vamps can see better at night and a lot of people are happy with that.<br /> <br /> I wasn't citing any specifics of those, other than those were the first other types of vampires that sprang to mind. The only things that occur to me as being able to operate in pitch darkness are things that are blind anyway, so don't &quot;see&quot; at all. On a base level it's counter intuitive to me that if something can see, that darkness doesn't effect it.<br /> <br /> You say the Anti's are getting tangled up trying to justify why they don't like it, but it's just the same from here, does the lack of mechanics really take anything away from the game? Because it hasn't in any of the games i've played in.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T18:05:43-07:00","id":1304057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304049#post1304049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a base level it's counter intuitive to me that if something can see, that darkness doesn't effect it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's just an unsupported assumption based on personal bias. You're trying to make it sound like mythology supports your position, but you're essentially admitting to just name dropping types of vampires and ignored any of their supernatural qualities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...does the lack of mechanics really take anything away from the game? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Mechanics that don't support the game lore diminish the play experience. If my vampire is supposed to see better at night than humans, but the low-light penalty is the same for vampires and humans, then either the lore is wrong, or the mechanics are wrong, and one should change to stop taking away from the game by forcing us to address the contradiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it hasn't in any of the games i've played in. </div> </div> </div>In WtA 1e, there was a rule that was written poorly, and made werewolves unkillable if they take 1 bashing damage before any other damage. This spurned all the WoD game lines, even though VtM 1e and Mage 1e didn't have that problem, address in how damage works to ensure that didn't get repeated.<br /> <br /> So even if you never ran into this issue because you never played WtA 1e, fixing the problem most likely affected you because you've probably played a WoD besides VtM 1e and Mage 1e.<br /> <br /> Just because a bad rule hasn't impacted you, doesn't mean it shouldn't be fixed for the people it did affect, and doesn't mean it doesn't actually help you later down the line when that refinement gets incorporated into things you do use eventually.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T18:22:22-07:00","id":1304060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304057#post1304057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's just an unsupported assumption based on personal bias. You're trying to make it sound like mythology supports your position, but you're essentially admitting to just name dropping types of vampires and ignored any of their supernatural qualities.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not ignoring any supernatural qualities, i'm saying i've never heard this specific one attributed to them. Or anything outside dnd really. Which is what i was asked. This demand for a mechanic is reminding me of people complaining about a Katana's stats not being right. If you use a katana, then i get that it pisses you off, but the people that don't probably haven't even thought of it.<br /> <br /> I am curious about the WtA thing though, and how it impacted things. I'm not sure it's a fair comparison though. Not all rules are created equal, i'm just going to look at the grappling rules, which were <i>awful </i>in most of the editions. It's not something i feel the need to demand needs to be changed despite it having far more of an impact than any minor tweak to lowlight vision.<br /> <br /> But i think i get where you're coming from now, just really think there are better things that could be addressed. Especially given my very low opinion of V5 to start with.<br /> <br /> To answer the thread question with my opinion<br /> <br /> Most people didn't think it was needed or fitting in the setting<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":1037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","user":"jamiemalk","date":".  Slight rewording 04-10-2019, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T01:35:11-07:00","id":1304127,"title":"","content":"VTM mechanics never were good for starters , heck requiem 2ED rules supports better the setting of the masquerade than his own official rules.<br /> <br /> The saving point of masquerade were it shines as a TTRPG has always been his characters and setting but never his rules.<br /> <br /> The perfect example of this is bloodlines a buggy game where the combat was boring and uninteresting (damm sewers) but the characters interactions and plot where such a prize that we were more than willing to pay the prize falling in love with the NPCs in the process and for this it remains as one of my favorite games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 04-11-2019, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T02:00:55-07:00","id":1304129,"title":"","content":"The idea that vampires can't see well in low light conditions<br /> <br /> 1. Is not supported by decades of fluff.<br /> 2. Fails to take into account how incredibly impractical, not to mention wildly dangerous unlife would have been for non protean/auspex having neonates in the period streching from the first city to early 20th century. Letters would not been written or read (unless you were standing close to that giant fire place) and the sheer, everyday amount of quickly escalatable danger that would befall someone who spent their every waking moment with vision based penalites whilst living a life of conspiracy, stealth, stalking and violence, sabotages any attempt to suspend disbelief.<br /> <br /> I also personally think that vampires with flashlights and IR-goggles are a huge moodbreaker. I want my vampires clad in cool, slightly impractical clothes, not riot gear. I want my vampires soaking damage with undead stamina and fortitude, not bullet proof vests. I want my vampires to fight with rending claws, flashing teeth and the occasional sword, not with M60s and phosphorous grenades. I want my vampires to see in the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T07:51:52-07:00","id":1304191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304049#post1304049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the dim/pitch thing that seems to be the breaking point. A lot of people, myself included, don't really think dim light is as big of an issue as other people. As you say, it's just not something that's generally highlighted.<b> As with the Revised write up, it says vamps can see better at night and a lot of people are happy with that.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So, what you're saying it's that you do agree that vampires can see better in the dark than humans? Or you're saying that this fluff <i>shouldn't</i> have been part of Revised? You're against vampires seeing better in the dark than humans or just don't want it <i><b>ruled</b></i>?.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe one more thing and they'd offically tip over into a VtR game.<br /> <br /> The more distance between the gamelines the better, others may like it but i'd prefer VtM to stay as much out of VtR as it can. </div> </div> </div>Your argument here leaves me baffled: Complete Darkvision would be the last straw that would turn V5 into VtR?, T<b>hat </b>would be the last straw and not the Touchstones or the changes to vampiric society. Everyone that defends this inhability it's, at the same time, saying that <i>they scarcely apply it</i>. You yourself say that darkness it's never a serious issue in your games.<br /> <br /> For most people that think V5 it's too similar to VtR, that &quot;last straw&quot; was droped a long time ago. For people that think V5 isn't that similar to VtR <i>yet</i>, I would really need to ask: why would something so insignificat be &quot;the last straw&quot;, if you honestly accept everything else?.<br /> <br /> If you just generally don't want VtR on Masquerade (and thus that last straw was dropped long ago), it's better to say so instead of defending this lack of a rule as an strategic choice to prevent V5 requiemization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">]If there is too much darkness in your chronicle that you need powers to see in the dark, hopefully that is intentional design by your Storyteller for the mood he's trying to create, otherwise he's just doing a bad job and punishing you for not being able to see in the dark. And you should get a different storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're ignoring my arguments. I said explicitly that the probelm it's that <b>nobody </b>uses this &quot;curse&quot; as a serious deal. You don't see STs pretending that Hunger or Sunlight don't exist. STs will ALWAYS find a way to mix these elements with the plot to make the Curse relevant. Yet STs will often ignore darkness. If your vampires see at night as well and as far as mages see with daylight and never experience a problem <u>then darkness it's not a factor</u>. Your vampires &quot;see well in the dark&quot; already.<br /> <br /> You're doing something worse than transforming this abstract rules debate into MY problem. YOURE FABRICATING A PROBLEM THAT DOESN'T EXIST...I know that somethimes it's tempting to make a strawman. Heck, sometimes it may even help to explain a point by comparison. I'm not an anti-fallacy fundamentalist. But what you're doing isn't that, you're ignoring my side of the argument completely.<br /> <br /> This it's not even part of your argument, and I find it insluting because it implies I'm debating this because I'm projecting a problem I have in my table, instead of being an abstract consideration about the rules. I'm going to chose to believe it wasn't intentional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Vampire lore, it seems likely that vampires received disciplines after the curse, NOT because of it. .</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're doing here it's called &quot;cherry-picking&quot;. I didn't mentioned just Disciplines as boons of the Curse.<br /> <br /> I also mentioned: being immortal, unaging, immune to most diseases, capable of making yourself stronger, faster and more resistant, heal most wounds, and enslave people to your blood.<br /> <br /> All of this alone it's enough to make vampires, as <i>Cifer</i> points, &quot;clearly superhuman&quot;. Even without having learned a single Discipline.<br /> <br /> So, to be clear:<b> The fact that vampires get a lot of powers with Curse of Caine as an inherent part of becoming a vampire remains true regardless if these were created before or after the Curse, and regardless how many horrendous downsides the Curse may have.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If this is the case, the 'Curse of Caine' is fitting as it banishes you to darkness in a world where there is only torchlight to see by which you are terrified of. And your fellow man who might keep you compay in this new dark world? You eat him. Eternally banished to walk the earth in darkness and eat people, and to be afraid of the only light source you are able to use... THAT is a punishment. So no, I don't think that anything compensates for the curse. With the disciplines coming after the curse, being given by another source, the point of the curse was just that. To curse. God gave no compensation or mercy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's incredibly frustrating to me that you've written this beautifully composed <b><i>strawman:</i></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>WoD Vampires have a lot of problems</b>, <i>but they also have a lot of powers humans don't get</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying vampires shouldn't be hungry or lonely, so please don't muddle the field with aspects of the Curse that I'm not questioning at all.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm not even saying that Caine Himself was cursed with all those cool powers</b>, the &quot;Curse of Caine&quot; isn't just what Caine suffered but a way to refer to the vampiric state itself. And you were using it that way, you weren't talking about Caine before but about &quot;vampires as cursed humans&quot;. <i>And being a vampire certainly does come with a lot of perks</i>.<br /> <br /> You can always say that &quot;to see better in the dark than humans&quot; was a power that Caine got AFTER being cursed, like the Blood Bond, if you think it's cool for the curse to be to roam the world at darkness with prey eyes, and that it should have no benefits by itself. Maybe Caine become the greatest predator latter. It's headcanon but it would conflict less with the lore than vampires not being able to see better in the dark.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it wasn't intended for vampires to have so many cool <b>inherent </b>powers (God ain't so Omniscient, it seems). But the point here that you're avoiding <i>it's that vampires do have a lot of cool powers</i> that come with &quot;being a vampire&quot;. I was merely saying that havig superhuman powers goes side by side with being a Vampire, and being able to see in the dark could be one of them.<br /> <br /> So, let me get this straight: Vampires are <b>inherently </b>MORE than able to subdue a human and eat him with superpowers, and that's not a blessing because you need to eat people and that's bad...but making vampires able to <i>see in the dark</i> to perform this activity even better would be too much and make the condition desirable?<br /> <br /> See how your argument doesn't really adress my argument?: You merely made a very good looking idea(Caine was cursed to be blind in the dark and alone, he doesn't get cool powers for being cursed) that has nothing to do with being a regular Cainite (who do have loads of powers that come with their condition and never seen having problems with the dark). One thing has <i>nothing</i> to do with the other.<br /> <br /> Also, a nitpick: as has been mentioned in this thread, torches aren't a good way to see in the dark unless there's total darkness. Which in outdoors it's pretty rare. So keeping your human eyes it's not that bad of a curse, it's more a situational problem that you would get accustomed to, eventually (and, in my opinion, not very aesthetical or interesting from a narrative standpoint. Hence it's never used)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I'm not arguing for players to be punished while in the dark. My point seems to be missed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here we're debating that there should be arule about not punishing players while in the dark. Because RPG have rules to rule things out. The fluff was there until V5 took it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowledgeseeker</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just arguing why the it seems logical that the curse of Caine would exclude vampires from being able to naturally see in the dark. I'm rationalizing here BECAUSE vampires CAN'T see in the dark naturally. My arguments stem from being able to strategically use darkness in storytelling for mood, and for lore and role play reasons. Makes sense to me. Maybe it does't make sense to everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that we've clarified that the Curse of Caine doesn't refers solely to Caine himself and that those that bear it, vampires, have a LOT of blessings that come with it, I can ask again: why should it exclude them from being able to see like a predator in the dark if it doesn't exclude them from being dominant over humans in a lot of other ways?<br /> <br /> Nobody it's arguing against vampires being in eternal darkness, people it's arguing against vampires being bad at living in eternal darkness.<br /> <br /> I thin that you want to fabricate the idea that the Curse should somehow include notbeing able to see in the dark. Which clearly isn't the case: Not only this isn't mentioned anywhere, but also clashes with Revised fluff and there's the fact that no other aspect of the Curse can be nulified so easily (no level 1 Disciplines was ever able to override sunlight or fire vulnerabilities). In fact, you yourself think vampires in general should have no problem with that unwritten aspect of the Curse you fabricated! , so you would have to forgive me if I fail to see the problem of making that a rule!<br /> <br /> <b>Mood </b>benefits from vampires stalking humans without needing lanterns, <b>lore </b>points towards the idea that vampires do see better in the night than humans, and <b>role play</b>ers that I have seen never, ever, roleplay not being able to function in the night as they would function in daylight (not recognizing faces until they're close or clearly illuminated, not knowing if the dude they're stalking it's red haired because there's not much ligth in that place)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-11-2019, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T09:22:31-07:00","id":1304219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304191#post1304191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, what you're saying it's that you do agree that vampires can see better in the dark than humans? Or you're saying that this fluff <i>shouldn't</i> have been part of Revised? You're against vampires seeing better in the dark than humans or just don't want it <i><b>ruled</b></i>?.</div> </div> </div> </div>No rule, basically. The fluff is more than enough. Like i said, this is just like arguing over DnD Katana stats to me. It's a corner case thing that anybody can reasonably cope with in the system without a static number, and i feel a static number would lessen things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304191#post1304191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your argument here leaves me baffled: Complete Darkvision would be the last straw that would turn V5 into VtR?, T<b>hat </b>would be the last straw and not the Touchstones or the changes to vampiric society. Everyone that defends this inhability it's, at the same time, saying that <i>they scarcely apply it</i>. You yourself say that darkness it's never a serious issue in your games.<br /> <br /> For most people that think V5 it's too similar to VtR, that &quot;last straw&quot; was droped a long time ago. For people that think V5 isn't that similar to VtR <i>yet</i>, I would really need to ask: why would something so insignificat be &quot;the last straw&quot;, if you honestly accept everything else?.<br /> <br /> If you just generally don't want VtR on Masquerade (and thus that last straw was dropped long ago), it's better to say so instead of defending this lack of a rule as an strategic choice to prevent V5 requiemization.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if i could remove all the Requiem stuff that would be awesome, so obviously any more Requiem is bad from where i'm sitting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:33:19-07:00","id":1304271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304219#post1304219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No rule, basically. The fluff is more than enough. Like i said, this is just like arguing over DnD Katana stats to me. It's a corner case thing that anybody can reasonably cope with in the system without a static number, and i feel a static number would lessen things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough, the abilities that do exist tend to have system numbers. Is Eyes of the Beast a bad thing for noting that it provides an Intimidation bonus of 2 dice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304219#post1304219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if i could remove all the Requiem stuff that would be awesome, so obviously any more Requiem is bad from where i'm sitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying things become bad when Requiem uses them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T12:05:36-07:00","id":1304282,"title":"","content":"While I will definitely acknowledge I'm on the &quot;V5 moved too much towards VtR,&quot; camp, very little of it is the mechanics that bother me. Touchstones bug me mechanically for not being more VtR-like, because I feel their current V5 implementation is a compromise that loses all the good parts of VtR's Touchstones, and doesn't help how VtM has traditionally approached fending off the Beast.<br /> <br /> To me it's pretty simple. If a change of rules would make V5 unambiguously better... it shouldn't matter if it came from VtR, or anywhere else. Not having a better play experience with a game just to spite an emotional concept (to be specific, the concept of &quot;Requiemization&quot; here)... is something that just does not compute for me.<br /> <br /> In this specific thing, vampire &quot;physiology&quot; between VtM and VtR has never been a significant difference between the games. The idea that better rules for either game-line is going to make them look a bit more similar shouldn't really be a surprise or a problem. The differences have always been strongest and most important to the fans in where things go from there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T12:21:35-07:00","id":1304287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying things become bad when Requiem uses them?</div> </div> </div> </div>XD. I completely understand there are people that want to see Requiem out of V5. I'm pretty much on the &quot;V5 moved too much towards VtR&quot; camp too. At least in my case it's not that &quot;Requiem makes things bad&quot; as much as &quot;Masquerade has a different feel and that's good&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't think most people on that camp thinks rules are bad if Requiem uses them. I mean, we would need to leave the d10 mechanics in that case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But your way of puting it it's still funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T02:39:07-07:00","id":1304419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1256687#post1256687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becuase they wanted night vision to be a protean 1 power wich is a same becuase they could have give you something cool.In requiem nigh vision is an standard power becuase the beast is a creature of the dark and protean theme is metmorphosis and the hability to steal natural adaptations from other predators.<br /> <br /> If you want to know more about protean in Requiem 2ED it was open devolopment so you can consult the discipline here<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1juI7Er1pUnl79v9zt8NCu4q6jynnCGKJvMZwHJHot7s/pub\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...MZwHJHot7s/pub</a><br /> <br /> The beuty and versatibility of the disciplines in VTR 2ED is something unseen in all the Vampire games from V5 to V1.They also were balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to each his or her own.<br /> I prefer the 3rd/V5 version of the Protean discipline. I would never had loved Vampire if Reqium was the only ersion. I bought the books, laughed at all the pathetic sillyness and sent them back to the store to get a refund. I wont touch those silly clans and Covenants with a 10 ft pole nor the Protean power.<br /> <br /> To me it felt that White Wolf had the following line of thought when they made Reqium:<br /> <br /> WW vd: For the last 9-10 years we have made one of the most successful gamelines in Tabletop RPG games ever. Our fans love our books and LARPs. What can we do now that we put Gehenna into the mix?<br /> <br /> WW idea man: Hmm, we make a new vampire game and reuse almost everything so we do not have to work that much<br /> <br /> ww vd: what you mean? <br /> <br /> WW idea man: We still need clans, change the names on a few of them, keep a few but remove or change a letter: Malkavians become Malkovians, Toreador becomes Daeva...<br /> <br /> WW vd: but people like Toreador?<br /> <br /> WW idea man: make Toreador a daeva bloodlie!<br /> <br /> WW vd: Oh ok.<br /> <br /> ww idea man: We keep Brujah, Giovanni (but add a san before their name sp people wont get it, And Niktucu becomes Nictocu, that is subtle enough...<br /> <br /> WW vd: What about disciplines<br /> <br /> ww idea man : Make all see in the datk ot that it is needed for a modern urban predator with all the lights in the cities at night, and change them just a bit, Instead of seeing in the dark, make gangrel sprout thousands of insectoid legs so they can climb on ceilings, for that is howvampires do it.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Reqium was probably the worst vampire game ever created by WW. Even KotE and THe African Kindred books were good in comparsion. Req could had been so much better if they had made a totally new game, not reused anything. But as it was recycled from 1st - 3rd edition, WW lost so many old fas who like me looked at the books and scoffed at them. New players who started after Req 1st edition only had that to go on and did not know any other games.<br /> <br /> So Req ruined VtM for a decade before V5 came out. V5 is not heavensent but it is at least an OK version of the real vampire game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24695-little_miss_-serneholt","name":"Little_Miss_ Serneholt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T06:22:35-07:00","id":1304436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304191#post1304191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thin that you want to fabricate the idea that the Curse should somehow include not being able to see in the dark. Which clearly isn't the case: Not only this isn't mentioned anywhere, but also clashes with Revised fluff</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's in the book, then it's settled. I didn't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304191#post1304191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thin that you want to fabricate the idea that the Curse should somehow include not being able to see in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that Vampires didn't see any differently in the dark than people to any meaningful degree, therefore I was <i>rationalizing </i>why that would be the case. Using examples of why it would make sense. I was backing up the book (and what I thought had a lack of clarification) and defending the lore. Now that I know it's in a book somewhere, I don't really care. I was wrong. <b>The only thing I ever cared about is Storytellers using darkness as a tool for mood. </b>My stance was that if you magically make them see in the dark (when I believed they couldn't - and absolutely not because of the curse, it's not an extra punishment levied on them), you're cutting out an important part of what it is to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304191#post1304191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strawman</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not going there. Using strawman against someone is akin to knowing their intentions. <br /> <br /> Good job on your win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T10:39:18-07:00","id":1304462,"title":"","content":"OK, so important bit on theme and mood? A core part of VtM is the struggle to remain human. Everything that pushes vampires to overlook how inhuman they've become is helping set the mood of the game.<br /> <br /> Having &quot;blood senses&quot; ala VtR 2e? It's all about that mood. It's not perfect dark-senses, but it's a nice boost. What you can sense when to comes to blood is the big boost... and wonderful for mood. Every vampire walking down the street is constantly reminded they're a predator walking past walking meals. The thrum of heart beats constantly reminding them of all that tasty blood flowing around. The warmth of human skin is carried by the blood. Those odd colored drops on asphalt everyone is ignoring? Blood. You can smell the misty blood on the air as some human is getting pummeled in the dark of an alley... it would be so easy to follow the trail and use the dark to sneak up on the mugger and be a hero... and snack on that asshole. Or just have it easy and sulk in the shadows, waiting for the violent blood soaked hands to leave you a gift wrapped meal laying in the shadow of a dumpster.<br /> <br /> You want mood? That's way more important than trying to make vampires uneasy because it's pitch black outside. Sure there's all sorts of practical uses to it, but it helps twist a vampire to see humans as kine. As meals carrying precious, precious blood... because just like drinking blood has taken over for hunger or other physical needs, sensing blood is now how they feel the world. They can never escape it.<br /> <br /> Want to make things scary? The vampires go into a place and all those blood senses? They pick up nothing. No humans... no dogs... no rats... no blood. Whatever lays in wait for them, whether the darkness conceals threats, or momentary scares, they know going forward means no way to slake their hunger, and every time they call on the blood, the Beast stirs a bit more, and there will be no respite coming soon.<br /> <br /> Darkness doesn't stop being a tool for mood if vampires have better night vision... it becomes a better one, but the mood is all about vampires struggling with the monsters they are, and the monsters they might become. The darkness isn't there to be a threat to their safety, but a threat to their humanity... because humans aren't at home in the dark, they don't see the world through blood tinted eyes, and they don't look at other humans and sense 'food' as their first thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-12-2019, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T13:14:12-07:00","id":1304490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Little_Miss_ Serneholt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304419#post1304419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Req ruined VtM for a decade before V5 came out. V5 is not heavensent but it is at least an OK version of the real vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This is edition warring, which is against rule 3 - respect other people\u2019s preferences. You are more that welcome to dislike Requiem, but dismissing it as not a real vampire game is not acceptable.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T08:31:19-07:00","id":1305482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1256606-why-didn-t-v5-make-see-in-the-dark-standard-for-all-vampires?p=1304490#post1304490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">This is edition warring, which is against rule 3 - respect other people\u2019s preferences. You are more that welcome to dislike Requiem, but dismissing it as not a real vampire game is not acceptable.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was not to disrespect others preferences it was just my opinion. I meant to say It was not a real/original cocept of the Vampire (as in The Masquerade) game.<br /> <br /> English is like my fifth language and while i try to my written or spoken language might not always convey what I want to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24695-little_miss_-serneholt","name":"Little_Miss_ Serneholt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T07:45:48-07:00","id":1487381,"title":"","content":"Here's how I'd redo Protean:<br /> Eyes of the Beast is gone. The ability to see in the dark is simply a racial.<br /> (1)Earth Meld. Earth Meld takes 3 full turns to balance its now lower level.<br /> (2)Unchanged.<br /> (3)Weight of the Feather, but without it's downsides. It is now simply the bonuses for a scene after making a rouse check.<br /> 4 and 5 unchanged.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}